B's blocked interval, 15.4 to 17.4 s, is the shared car-swept shot. It now draws the same rebuilt bank as A. That means:
- the far bank in broken, stepped blocks under an irregular grass edge;
- the toe that wanders and pushes out round 5 slumped blocks;
- the water's far edge following the toe, with no pale top band (lit .002, y0 bankY-20);
- CreekToe's broken shadows, reflections and foam;
- the irregular ledge waterline;
- the zigzag near-bank courses;
- the overlapping CreekShelf layers.
B's creek-plan (CreekPlan and the creek-plan case) is unchanged, and it was clean in round 24. CREEK_PLAN, CREEK_CAM, CREEK_CAR, S3 and the landmarks are unchanged, and all changed rows sit above the caption band. s4 is unchanged: no lit prop, the same ext and the same floodFoot.
